# JA-Mail AI governance

## Dependency

Mail AI **requires** Core global AI (`Settings → AI` / Setting group `ai`):

1. `ai_enabled` must be true
2. Selected (or default) provider must have `{provider}_api_key`
3. Mail prefs: `ai_enabled` + `ai_scope_drafting`
4. Effective flag from API: `ai_ready`

Do not call `/manage/ai/generate` unless `ai_ready` is true.

## Live vs unavailable (kernel)

| Capability | Status |
|------------|--------|
| Drafting / polish in composer | **Live** |
| Summarize / smart reply / sentiment | **Unavailable** — keep switches locked off; do not ship fake UI |
| Human-in-the-loop | **Always on** — AI never auto-sends |
| PII masking | Live client-side redact before prompt when enabled |

## Agent rules

- Never present unavailable scopes as working product.
- Never invent IMAP/SPF/DKIM AI features.
- Prefer `AiAvailability` (PHP) / `useAiAvailability` (FE) / mail `ai_ready`.
- Core `AiController::generate` must refuse when global AI is off (`AI_DISABLED`).
- Update `docs/extensions/ja-mail.md` + Mail CHANGELOGs when AI behavior changes.
